    "title": "Ohio National Guard deploying Saturday - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Carlos Mathis ,\n13 hours ago\nCOLUMBUS, Ohio ( WDTN ) -- Over 100 members of the Ohio Army National Guard are deploying this weekend.\nThe OANG confirmed approximately 120 members of its 1191st Engineer Company are heading to the U.S. southern border to support Operation Ardent Vanguard.\n\"While deployed, the unit will provide operational support as part of Operation Ardent\nVanguard, which encompasses U.S. Northern Command efforts to secure the border against\nunlawful mass migration, narcotics trafficking, human smuggling, and other criminal activities,\" said OANG.\nA call of duty ceremony will be held Saturday, Oct. 17 at 11 a.m. in Portsmouth.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDTN.com.\n110",
    "summary": "The OANG confirmed approximately 120 members of its 1191st Engineer Company are heading to the U.S. southern border to support Operation Ardent Vanguard. \"While deployed, the unit will provide operational support as part of Operation Ardent Vanguard, which encompasses U.S. Northern Command efforts to secure the border against unlawful mass migration, narcotics trafficking, human smuggling, and other criminal activities,\" said OANG. A call of duty ceremony will be held Saturday, Oct. 17 at 11 a.m. in Portsmouth. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WDTN.com.",
